\textbf{Estimating net change from a rate-of-change function:}
\begin{enumerate}
\item Choose the number of rectangles $n$ and compute $\Delta t=\frac{\text{end}-\text{start}}{n}$.
\item Choose left endpoints, right endpoints, or midpoints to evaluate the rate function on each subinterval.
\item Approximate $\text{Net Change}\approx \sum f(\text{sample point})\cdot \Delta t$.
\item Left- and right-endpoint estimates typically bracket the true value. The exact net change is the definite integral.
\end{enumerate}

